> north
Hall

The hall is narrow, but the polished key throws a small gleam ahead.

You can see a caretaker.

Available exits: south.

The floorboards answer your first step with a tired creak.
!chapter study
!scene polished_key

> talk to caretaker
"That key remembers more doors than this house has left," the caretaker says.

> ask caretaker about key
"It was cut for the study before the study had a name," the caretaker says.

> show key to caretaker
The caretaker turns the polished key toward the light and nods once.

> ask caretaker about house
"The house remembers every hand that closes a door," the caretaker says.

> tell caretaker about old house
"Then it remembers you now," the caretaker says.

> flip key
The key lands teeth-up in your palm.

> give key to caretaker
"Keep it," the caretaker says. "It has chosen your pocket."
